 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Customer Purchase Behaviour Analysis (Project DA-002)\n",
    "## Category: Customer Analytics | Currency: Indian Rupees (₹)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective\n",
    "Explore customer transactional records to identify purchasing patterns, evaluate order frequency and spending behavior, compare rule-based customer segments, discover top products, and assess repeat-purchase loyalty. This notebook produces customer-level summaries, segment comparisons, data visualizations, and evidence-grounded business recommendations to support customer retention, loyalty initiatives, and targeted marketing campaigns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Library Imports\n",
    "Import standard analytical and visualization libraries: Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"muted\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams['font.sans-serif'] = 'DejaVu Sans'\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 120\n",
    "print(\"Libraries successfully imported.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data Loading\n",
    "Load customer transaction data from CSV (or optional Excel format). Notice that this dataset is a clearly labeled synthetic/demonstration dataset created for Project DA-002."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load synthetic transaction dataset\n",
    "data_path = \"../data/transactions.csv\"\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    df_raw = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded {len(df_raw)} raw transaction records from {data_path}.\")\n",
    "except Exception:\n",
    "    # Fallback if working directory is root\n",
    "    df_raw = pd.read_csv(\"data/transactions.csv\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded {len(df_raw)} raw transaction records from data/transactions.csv.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_raw.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Data Cleaning and Hygiene Pipeline\n",
    "Enforce strict data validation rules:\n",
    "- Drop rows with missing or blank `customer_id`.\n",
    "- Parse dates into ISO format; drop invalid or corrupt date records.\n",
    "- Deduplicate identical transaction rows.\n",
    "- Validate numeric quantity (> 0) and unit price (>= 0).\n",
    "- Calculate missing `amount` using `quantity * unit_price` ONLY when both inputs are valid.\n",
    "- Clean and normalize whitespace in product names.\n",
    "- Record all dropped rows and cleaning reasons without arbitrary data imputation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_raw = len(df_raw)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Deduplication\n",
    "df_dedup = df_raw.drop_duplicates(subset=['transaction_id'] if 'transaction_id' in df_raw.columns else None)\n",
    "duplicate_count = total_raw - len(df_dedup)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Missing customer_id\n",
    "missing_cust_mask = df_dedup['customer_id'].isna() | (df_dedup['customer_id'].astype(str).str.strip() == '')\n",
    "missing_customer_count = missing_cust_mask.sum()\n",
    "df_valid_cust = df_dedup[~missing_cust_mask].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Date validation\n",
    "df_valid_cust['parsed_date'] = pd.to_datetime(df_valid_cust['transaction_date'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "invalid_date_count = df_valid_cust['parsed_date'].isna().sum()\n",
    "df_valid_date = df_valid_cust[df_valid_cust['parsed_date'].notna()].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Quantity and Unit Price sanitization\n",
    "df_valid_date['quantity'] = pd.to_numeric(df_valid_date['quantity'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df_valid_date['unit_price'] = pd.to_numeric(df_valid_date['unit_price'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df_valid_date['amount'] = pd.to_numeric(df_valid_date['amount'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Amount calculation: when missing or <= 0, recalculate if qty > 0 and unit_price > 0\n",
    "calc_mask = (df_valid_date['amount'].isna() | (df_valid_date['amount'] <= 0)) & (df_valid_date['quantity'] > 0) & (df_valid_date['unit_price'] > 0)\n",
    "calculated_amounts_count = calc_mask.sum()\n",
    "df_valid_date.loc[calc_mask, 'amount'] = df_valid_date.loc[calc_mask, 'quantity'] * df_valid_date.loc[calc_mask, 'unit_price']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Invalid amounts dropped\n",
    "valid_amount_mask = df_valid_date['amount'].notna() & (df_valid_date['amount'] > 0) & (df_valid_date['quantity'] > 0)\n",
    "invalid_amount_count = (~valid_amount_mask).sum()\n",
    "df_clean = df_valid_date[valid_amount_mask].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Product name sanitization\n",
    "df_clean['product_name'] = df_clean['product_name'].astype(str).str.strip()\n",
    "df_clean.sort_values(by='parsed_date', inplace=True)\n",
    "df_clean.reset_index(drop=True, inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data cleaning complete. Retained {len(df_clean)} of {total_raw} rows ({len(df_clean)/total_raw*100:.1f}%).\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Data Quality and Hygiene Report\n",
    "Transparently audit data issues detected and cleaning decisions taken."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "quality_report = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Total Raw Transactions\", \"Count\": total_raw},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Duplicate Transactions Removed\", \"Count\": int(duplicate_count)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Missing Customer ID Rows Dropped\", \"Count\": int(missing_customer_count)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Invalid Date Rows Dropped\", \"Count\": int(invalid_date_count)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Invalid/Zero Amount Rows Dropped\", \"Count\": int(invalid_amount_count)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Missing Amounts Calculated (Qty x Unit Price)\", \"Count\": int(calculated_amounts_count)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Cleaned Valid Transactions\", \"Count\": len(df_clean)},\n",
    "    {\"Metric\": \"Data Retention Rate\", \"Count\": f\"{len(df_clean)/total_raw*100:.2f}%\"}\n",
    "])\n",
    "quality_report"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Customer Aggregation and Metrics\n",
    "Aggregate customer behavior metrics:\n",
    "- Unique order count (using `order_id` if present, never assuming each transaction row is a separate order).\n",
    "- Total spending in Indian Rupees (₹).\n",
    "- Average Order Value ($AOV = \\text{Customer Total Spend} / \\text{Customer Unique Orders}$).\n",
    "- Total quantity purchased.\n",
    "- First and last purchase dates.\n",
    "- Days since last purchase (recency relative to max dataset date).\n",
    "- Count of unique products purchased.\n",
    "- Repeat-purchase status (True if unique orders $\\ge 2$, else False)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "as_of_date = df_clean['parsed_date'].max()\n",
    "\n",
    "cust_records = []\n",
    "for cust_id, group in df_clean.groupby('customer_id'):\n",
    "    unique_orders = group['order_id'].nunique() if 'order_id' in group.columns else group['transaction_id'].nunique()\n",
    "    total_spend = group['amount'].sum()\n",
    "    total_qty = group['quantity'].sum()\n",
    "    unique_products = group['product_name'].nunique()\n",
    "    first_date = group['parsed_date'].min()\n",
    "    last_date = group['parsed_date'].max()\n",
    "    days_since_last = (as_of_date - last_date).days\n",
    "    aov = total_spend / unique_orders if unique_orders > 0 else 0.0\n",
    "    is_repeat = unique_orders >= 2\n",
    "    \n",
    "    cust_records.append({\n",
    "        'customer_id': cust_id,\n",
    "        'unique_orders': unique_orders,\n",
    "        'total_spend': round(total_spend, 2),\n",
    "        'average_order_value': round(aov, 2),\n",
    "        'total_quantity': int(total_qty),\n",
    "        'unique_products_count': unique_products,\n",
    "        'first_purchase_date': first_date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'),\n",
    "        'last_purchase_date': last_date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d'),\n",
    "        'days_since_last_purchase': days_since_last,\n",
    "        'is_repeat_buyer': is_repeat\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_customers = pd.DataFrame(cust_records)\n",
    "print(f\"Customer aggregation completed for {len(df_customers)} unique customers.\")\n",
    "df_customers.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Configurable Spending Segmentation\n",
    "Demonstration spending thresholds:\n",
    "- **Low Spend**: Below ₹5,000\n",
    "- **Medium Spend**: ₹5,000 to below ₹20,000\n",
    "- **High Spend**: ₹20,000 or above\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: These are demonstrative thresholds for exploratory segmentation, not universal business standards.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "LOW_THRESHOLD = 5000.0\n",
    "HIGH_THRESHOLD = 20000.0\n",
    "\n",
    "def assign_segment(spend):\n",
    "    if spend < LOW_THRESHOLD:\n",
    "        return 'Low Spend'\n",
    "    elif spend < HIGH_THRESHOLD:\n",
    "        return 'Medium Spend'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'High Spend'\n",
    "\n",
    "df_customers['spending_segment'] = df_customers['total_spend'].apply(assign_segment)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inactive high-spender flag: High spend segment and no purchase for >= 90 days\n",
    "df_customers['is_inactive_high_spender'] = (\n",
    "    (df_customers['spending_segment'] == 'High Spend') & \n",
    "    (df_customers['days_since_last_purchase'] >= 90)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Segment breakdown:\")\n",
    "print(df_customers['spending_segment'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Segment Comparison and Metrics Summary\n",
    "Calculate for each segment:\n",
    "- Customer count & percentage of customer base\n",
    "- Total segment revenue (₹)\n",
    "- Revenue contribution percentage (% of total sales)\n",
    "- Average spend per customer (₹)\n",
    "- Average order value (₹)\n",
    "- Repeat-purchase rate (%)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_revenue = df_customers['total_spend'].sum()\n",
    "total_cust_count = len(df_customers)\n",
    "\n",
    "segment_summary = []\n",
    "for seg in ['Low Spend', 'Medium Spend', 'High Spend']:\n",
    "    sub = df_customers[df_customers['spending_segment'] == seg]\n",
    "    cust_count = len(sub)\n",
    "    seg_rev = sub['total_spend'].sum()\n",
    "    seg_orders = sub['unique_orders'].sum()\n",
    "    repeat_count = sub['is_repeat_buyer'].sum()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    segment_summary.append({\n",
    "        'Segment': seg,\n",
    "        'Customer Count': cust_count,\n",
    "        'Customer Share (%)': round(cust_count / total_cust_count * 100, 1),\n",
    "        'Total Revenue (₹)': round(seg_rev, 2),\n",
    "        'Revenue Share (%)': round(seg_rev / total_revenue * 100, 1) if total_revenue > 0 else 0,\n",
    "        'Avg Spend / Customer (₹)': round(seg_rev / cust_count, 2) if cust_count > 0 else 0,\n",
    "        'Avg Order Value (₹)': round(seg_rev / seg_orders, 2) if seg_orders > 0 else 0,\n",
    "        'Repeat Purchase Rate (%)': round(repeat_count / cust_count * 100, 1) if cust_count > 0 else 0\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df_segment_summary = pd.DataFrame(segment_summary)\n",
    "df_segment_summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Product-Level Analytics\n",
    "Identify:\n",
    "- Top 10 products by revenue (₹)\n",
    "- Top 10 products by quantity sold\n",
    "- Unique buyers per product"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_product_summary = df_clean.groupby('product_name').agg(\n",
    "    total_revenue=('amount', 'sum'),\n",
    "    units_sold=('quantity', 'sum'),\n",
    "    unique_buyers=('customer_id', 'nunique'),\n",
    "    transactions=('transaction_id', 'count')\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "df_top_revenue = df_product_summary.sort_values(by='total_revenue', ascending=False).head(10).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "df_top_quantity = df_product_summary.sort_values(by='units_sold', ascending=False).head(10).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Top 10 Products by Revenue (₹) ===\")\n",
    "display(df_top_revenue)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Top 10 Products by Quantity Sold ===\")\n",
    "display(df_top_quantity)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Repeat-Purchase Analysis and Order Cadence\n",
    "Compare one-time buyers versus repeat buyers:\n",
    "- Repeat-purchase rate across customer base.\n",
    "- Revenue generated by repeat buyers vs. one-time buyers.\n",
    "- Average days elapsed between consecutive orders."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "repeat_mask = df_customers['is_repeat_buyer']\n",
    "num_repeat = int(repeat_mask.sum())\n",
    "num_onetime = int((~repeat_mask).sum())\n",
    "repeat_rate = (num_repeat / total_cust_count) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "rev_repeat = df_customers.loc[repeat_mask, 'total_spend'].sum()\n",
    "rev_onetime = df_customers.loc[~repeat_mask, 'total_spend'].sum()\n",
    "repeat_rev_share = (rev_repeat / total_revenue) * 100 if total_revenue > 0 else 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate inter-order cadence in days for repeat buyers\n",
    "cadence_days = []\n",
    "for cust_id, group in df_clean.groupby('customer_id'):\n",
    "    # Get distinct order dates\n",
    "    order_dates = sorted(group['parsed_date'].drop_duplicates())\n",
    "    if len(order_dates) >= 2:\n",
    "        for i in range(1, len(order_dates)):\n",
    "            diff = (order_dates[i] - order_dates[i-1]).days\n",
    "            if diff >= 0:\n",
    "                cadence_days.append(diff)\n",
    "\n",
    "avg_cadence = float(np.mean(cadence_days)) if cadence_days else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total Customers: {total_cust_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Repeat Buyers: {num_repeat} ({repeat_rate:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"One-Time Buyers: {num_onetime} ({100 - repeat_rate:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Repeat Buyer Revenue: ₹{rev_repeat:,.2f} ({repeat_rev_share:.1f}% of total)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average Days Between Orders: {avg_cadence:.1f} days\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Monthly Revenue Trends\n",
    "Aggregate monthly sales performance over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_clean['month_year'] = df_clean['parsed_date'].dt.to_period('M')\n",
    "monthly_trends = df_clean.groupby('month_year').agg(\n",
    "    revenue=('amount', 'sum'),\n",
    "    orders=('order_id', 'nunique') if 'order_id' in df_clean.columns else ('transaction_id', 'count'),\n",
    "    active_customers=('customer_id', 'nunique')\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "monthly_trends['month_str'] = monthly_trends['month_year'].astype(str)\n",
    "monthly_trends.sort_values(by='month_str', inplace=True)\n",
    "monthly_trends"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Visualizations with Matplotlib and Seaborn\n",
    "Render the 8 required analytical charts in Indian Rupees (₹)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(4, 2, figsize=(16, 20))\n",
    "plt.subplots_adjust(hspace=0.35, wspace=0.25)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Monthly Revenue Trend\n",
    "ax1 = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "ax1.plot(monthly_trends['month_str'], monthly_trends['revenue'] / 1e3, marker='o', color='#2563eb', linewidth=2.5)\n",
    "ax1.set_title('1. Monthly Revenue Trend (₹ in Thousands)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Month')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('Revenue (₹k)')\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\n",
    "for x, y in zip(monthly_trends['month_str'], monthly_trends['revenue'] / 1e3):\n",
    "    ax1.annotate(f'₹{y:.0f}k', (x, y), textcoords=\"offset points\", xytext=(0,6), ha='center', fontsize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Top 10 Products by Revenue\n",
    "ax2 = axes[0, 1]\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df_top_revenue, y='product_name', x='total_revenue', ax=ax2, palette='Blues_r')\n",
    "ax2.set_title('2. Top 10 Products by Revenue (₹)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax2.set_xlabel('Total Revenue (₹)')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Top 10 Products by Quantity\n",
    "ax3 = axes[1, 0]\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df_top_quantity, y='product_name', x='units_sold', ax=ax3, palette='Greens_r')\n",
    "ax3.set_title('3. Top 10 Products by Quantity Sold (Units)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax3.set_xlabel('Units Sold')\n",
    "ax3.set_ylabel('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Revenue by Customer Segment\n",
    "ax4 = axes[1, 1]\n",
    "seg_colors = {'Low Spend': '#94a3b8', 'Medium Spend': '#3b82f6', 'High Spend': '#10b981'}\n",
    "colors_list = [seg_colors.get(s, '#3b82f6') for s in df_segment_summary['Segment']]\n",
    "ax4.bar(df_segment_summary['Segment'], df_segment_summary['Total Revenue (₹)'] / 1e3, color=colors_list, width=0.5)\n",
    "ax4.set_title('4. Revenue by Customer Segment (₹k)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax4.set_ylabel('Revenue (₹k)')\n",
    "for idx, row in df_segment_summary.iterrows():\n",
    "    ax4.text(idx, (row['Total Revenue (₹)'] / 1e3) + 5, f\"{row['Revenue Share (%)']}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 5. Customers by Spending Segment\n",
    "ax5 = axes[2, 0]\n",
    "ax5.pie(\n",
    "    df_segment_summary['Customer Count'], \n",
    "    labels=df_segment_summary['Segment'], \n",
    "    autopct='%1.1f%%', \n",
    "    startangle=140, \n",
    "    colors=colors_list\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax5.set_title('5. Customer Base Share by Segment', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 6. Repeat vs One-Time Buyers\n",
    "ax6 = axes[2, 1]\n",
    "ax6.pie([num_repeat, num_onetime], labels=['Repeat Buyers', 'One-Time Buyers'], autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=90, colors=['#8b5cf6', '#cbd5e1'])\n",
    "ax6.set_title(f'6. Repeat vs One-Time Buyers ({repeat_rate:.1f}% Repeat Rate)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 7. Customer Spending Distribution\n",
    "ax7 = axes[3, 0]\n",
    "sns.histplot(df_customers['total_spend'], bins=20, kde=True, ax=ax7, color='#6366f1')\n",
    "ax7.set_title('7. Customer Spend Distribution (₹)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax7.set_xlabel('Total Customer Spend (₹)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 8. Purchase Frequency Distribution\n",
    "ax8 = axes[3, 1]\n",
    "order_counts = df_customers['unique_orders'].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "ax8.bar(order_counts.index.astype(str), order_counts.values, color='#0284c7', width=0.6)\n",
    "ax8.set_title('8. Purchase Frequency (Orders per Customer)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax8.set_xlabel('Number of Orders')\n",
    "ax8.set_ylabel('Number of Customers')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Customer-Level Summary Table & Inactive High Spender Flag\n",
    "Review top customers, identify repeat buyers, and inspect customers who have high historical spend but have been inactive (>= 90 days)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "inactive_high_spenders = df_customers[df_customers['is_inactive_high_spender']].sort_values(by='total_spend', ascending=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Identified {len(inactive_high_spenders)} inactive high-spending customers (>= ₹20,000 spend, >= 90 days inactive).\")\n",
    "inactive_high_spenders.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Evidence-Grounded Business Recommendations\n",
    "\n",
    "Based strictly on calculated figures from this dataset:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **High-Value Loyalty & Retention Program**:\n",
